{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact doc-links head 2680cbd0659fa1550ac8075af2d2b5a1c23d5630 on builder/doc-links-tracked-20261104, tree 58843462, for request cf33085f under promise b9c090fb and review request 7e043c67. This approval covers the scanner change, its test and the evidence.\n\nScope. Main bf3bceb6 is an ancestor, the worktree is clean, and the branch is pushed. The head changes scripts/check-doc-links.mjs, its test, the note and two manifests. Main has since gained the G3b packet 41771de1, which touches only notes under another directory. The commit-message check passes for both commits. No card path changes. From the gate commit 5cbd4535, tree 35b83756, only the note and the validation manifest change.\n\nWhat holds:\n\n- The scanner now lists paths with git ls-files --cached -z and reads their working bytes. It keeps the node_modules, .git and test exclusions, the notes rule (only notes/plans, and only with --history) and the spikes/parked rule. --self-test still exits before any Git call.\n- The new case keeps an ignored .builder-worktrees document and an untracked document, both with broken links, beside a tracked file whose name contains a space. The good link passes. Writing a broken link to the tracked file without staging it fails the check, so working bytes are what count.\n- The control restores the original scanner. The new case fails, with exit 1, and the existing canonical-link case still passes.\n- I ran the head's scanner against the shared checkout, which holds the nested worktrees: 1,028 local links, 0 broken, exit 0.\n\nThe gate passed. gate.exit at 5cbd4535 reads exit 0. Node ran 134 (one more than before, the new case), Counting 56, plain 3,607 with one skip and Native 1,070 with two skips.\n\nEvidence. The two manifests list 37 public files. All match their sizes and digests and are read-only, both SHA256SUMS files match, and no unit holds an unlisted file. The 39 selected private gate originals and the full 2,276-file inventory match their hashes and are read-only. The scan for private keys, GitHub tokens and bearer values finds no match. The note names both manifests' SHA-256 values, bfc1bb89… and b3bfdb25….\n\nArchitecture: sound. Git already knows which documents belong to the head, so asking Git replaces a directory walk that had to guess.\n\nSecurity: no finding. The script passes fixed arguments to git with execFileSync and no shell.\n\nSimplification: no required change. Two edges behave differently now, and both fail closed:\n\n1. A tracked Markdown file that someone deletes without git rm stays in the index. The scanner then throws ENOENT and exits 1 with a stack trace, where the old scanner simply skipped the file. I reproduced this in a scratch repository. The gate runs only in a clean checkout, so the gate never meets it, but a local run during editing does. Skipping index entries whose file is missing would match the old behavior.\n2. A root outside a Git repository now fails with \"not a git repository\". The old scanner walked it and passed. Only the self-test and the gate call the script, so nothing depends on that case today.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:17378a486ccae7f08e0c3301849961e9c15e6d3b","binding":"assigned","head":"2680cbd0659fa1550ac8075af2d2b5a1c23d5630","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f4a32ff23f79475c8d5667ec3e6a486e35cb2c71\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b9c090fbaadd1d9a9746a83486f659127679fa00\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:10601c623de55f7b827e0661a36403f134255eea","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}